From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matt Mower <mdmower@cmphys.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 12:10:52 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [feature-requests #1038] Compile a case range as one case
 with two bounds

createCaseRange() made one case and one label for each value of a case
range. When the cases of a switch statement have more values than a
jump table of the port can have, geniCodeSwitch() emits one comparison
for each case, and the time of the passes that follow grows with about
the third power of the number of comparisons. For mcs51, a range of
1024 values compiled in 18 seconds and a range of 2048 values in 135
seconds.

createCaseRange() now makes one case with one label, for the first
value of the range. The last value follows the first in the list of
switch values and has the new flag caseRangeEnd of struct value.
createCase() reports a duplicate case for a value inside a range.

geniCodeSwitch() emits two comparisons for a range. The new function
geniCodeCaseRange() omits the comparison with the first value when the
cases before the range have all lower values of the type of the
condition, and the comparison with a last value that is the highest
value of that type. geniCodeJumpTable() puts the label of a range into
the jump table once for each value. A range counts as two cases when
geniCodeJumpTable() compares the size of a jump table with the size of
the comparisons. For the test of --nosidechannels, which selects a jump
table for more than two cases, each value of a range counts as a case.

The change removes two faults of the loop in createCaseRange(). The
loop did not end for a range whose last value is INT_MAX. For a case
range that labels a statement outside a statement list, as in

    switch (n)
      case 2 ... 4:
        r = 1;

the grammar action of labeled_statement attached the statement to the
label of the last value and dropped the labels of the other values, and
the compiler stopped with a segmentation fault.

- A range such as case -3 ... 300 for an unsigned int, whose first
  value is above its last value after the conversion to the type of the
  condition, matches no value, as it did with a jump table. With
  comparisons it matched 0 to 300 and 65533 to 65535.
- copyValue() copies caseRangeEnd, which the copy of a switch statement
  in an inline function needs.
- ast_print() prints a range as one CASE line.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
